Methodology of the New Approach
In contrast to the proposed models of sustainable development, the authors create the model based on the following provisions: ñ Our system ñ the biosphere ñ is not closed and has the ability to perform external work, that is, it has the ability to evolve. ñ The evolution of inanimate nature, which preceded the emergence of life, was dominated by the processes of reducing free energy, which took the form of the second law of thermodynamics. ñ The evolution of living nature is dominated by processes that lead to an increase in free energy, which is true for all forms of life. Both of these processes determine the multidirectional evolution of inanimate and living nature and are controlled by the law of conservation of power. ñ Living systems (nature, society) with constant exchange with the environment should not be in equilibrium, that is, they must be capable of doing external work. The measure of the distance of a system from equilibrium is its free energy. For a living system, balance is death. ñ Any system cannot exist without interaction with its natural environment and combines two associated processes: an active flow of environmental impacts, which determines the capabilities or capacity of the system, and the use by society of the flow of resources resulting from this impact to meet needs. ñ The highway of evolution is an accelerating wave dynamic process from unstable equilibrium to stable non-equilibrium. ñ Sustainable innovative development of socio-economic systems is a chronoholistic process of growth in the useful capacity of the system with no increase in the rate of resource consumption while maintaining development in the face of negative external and internal influences. ñ The introduction of the ìpowerî measure into the project management of sustainable development makes it possible to establish a physically measurable relationship between needs and opportunities and formalize a system of natural-scientific parameters of sustainable innovative development. ñ The only way to increase the amount and density of solar energy retained on the Earth is human mental creative labor, which, with the help of more advanced machines and technologies, makes physical labor more productive. ñ The elementary scheme of the production cycle is determined by the equality: the total power at the input of the system is equal to the useful power plus the power of losses at the output. ñ A necessary and sufficient condition for the continuous development of society is people who are able to put forward and implement ideas that ensure the growth of societyís capabilities, the satisfaction of its needs, both non-vanishing and new. ñ A society that is able to use the creative innovative ideas of an individual to grow the opportunities of society as a whole and a society that uses its growth


