of opportunities to form such a creative individual will have the fastest growth rate of opportunities. ñ If, as a result of the implementation of creative ideas, society ensures a nondecreasing rate of growth in the efficiency of using the full consumed power not only for the present, but also in the future, then it will retain its development not only at the present time, but also in the future. Within the framework of the complex system theory, in accordance with the above provisions and with the aim to formalize the tasks of sustainable development, a methodology for managing sustainability has been developed using the approach of analyzing energy flows (power) changes in open and dynamic socio-economic systems (Jermolajeva & Trusina, 2021). Sustainable development is a continuous process of increasing the opportunities to meet the current needs of the existing socio-economic system in power measurements without compromising the ability to meet needs for future generations, while increasing the efficiency of using the full power of the system, reducing power losses and not increasing consumption in the face of negative external and internal influences (Bolshakov et al., 2019). Based on the above formulated concepts, in the frame of complex dynamic system and the power change analysis, an approach to the analysis of life open systems (Trusina & Jermolajeva, 2021) is formulated below: ó a complex socio-economic system, open to energy flows, meets all certain parameters and can be represented as a system of nested systems ñ the economic system is ëinvestedí in society and further surrounded by the natural system; ó the laws of economic growth and development of the ecological system determine the development of the economic system; ó input energy flows are directed from the external circuit; ó the value of total power, useful power, lost power and technological efficiency of the socio-economic system as a basis for constructing an invariant coordinate system; ó quality of life per inhabitant in terms of power as a function of the useful power of the socio-economic system (created as a result of activities), life expectancy and environmental quality. The quality of life characterizes the current present state and the potential for development in the future; ó the system of power change as a dynamic state and direction of development of the entire socio-economic system as a whole.
