The authors of the article also agree that one of the most important basic things for such changes to happen is educating people in various forms ñ formal education from kindergarten to university, informal education opportunities ñ courses, seminars, discussions, etc. There are various developments and proposals in the world, which should be implemented, while creating an interdisciplinary approach and explaining sustainability as a set of economic, social and ecological factors. It was concluded that the attraction of citizens and the successful use of their potential in specific territories are also important factors in ensuring sustainable development (Aleksejeva et al., 2018). And in this case too, it is necessary to educate people in the acquisition of knowledge and skills, as well as in the formation of civic self-awareness. However, in order to achieve changes in formal education, it is obviously necessary to improve the training of teachers themselves. There are several good examples of education systems in world practice, such as in Finland. Education is the main key to changing peopleís unsustainable lifestyles and through education we need to teach a way of systems thinking that every member of society can understand (Hofman-Bergholm, 2018).
Final Considerations
The changes taking place in the 21st century in various areas of life affect each person individually and society as a whole, as a result of which the understanding and attitude towards sustainability issues should also change. Therefore, it is necessary to develop and analyze different approaches, models and their interpretations in order to determine the most reasonable and effective means for real sustainability, and not only for determining sustainable development of country, for example, based on GDP in monetary terms, as it has been accepted in economic analysis for several decades. Development is sustainable in a certain cycle of the existence of a living system. In the transition between cycles, the chronointegrity of development is destroyed, dimensional gaps arise ñ crises that require breakthrough management technologies and sustainable development becomes a strategic goal of managing the way out of the crisis. Scientists and practitioners should deeply and comprehensively review and consider sustainable development in the nature-society-human system as development that conforms to the laws of global evolution of living nature and the laws of historical development of humankind. In accordance with the model for analyzing the power changes of the socio-economic system, the calculations of the total power energy resource consumption and GDP of the USA for the period of 1960ñ2021 were carried out. This example is an analysis of the development of the US socio-economic system in a new constant coordinate system in power units, and it can be concluded that the development is not as smooth as it appears when analyzing in monetary units. The authors of the article believe that the necessary changes in peopleís thinking and attitude can be changed mainly based on the education system throughout the life of a person and by introducing an increasingly broad and research-based interdisciplinary perspective on issues of sustainability and sustainable development.


